{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>He brought us out of the land of Egypt.</b> Rashi: 'His bringing us out was for hatred' etc. — that is, a rain-fed field is inferior to an irrigated one, because the rain-fed field bears produce only from rainwater, and when there is no rain it ceases; but the irrigated one never ceases, since they irrigate it constantly."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The comment appears to cite Rashi on this verse but expands the agricultural analogy (rain-fed vs. irrigated land) at length; the abbreviation וכו׳ is resolved as 'etc.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:48.378121245Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}